SECTION 16: DATA PROTECTION AND PRIVACY

16.1 In the course of providing the Services, the Service Provider may have access to personal data of the Client's employees, visitors, or other individuals. The Service Provider shall:

(a) Process such personal data only for the purposes of performing the Services and in accordance with the Client's documented instructions;

(b) Implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect such personal data against unauthorised or unlawful processing and against accidental loss, destruction, or damage;

